      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "6a96bb0674ef734037d3587a",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When we search for worlds, we usually look at the thumbnail to decide whether we want to visit.\n\nHowever, recently I’ve had many experiences where a world looked beautiful based on its thumbnail, but once I entered it, the world turned out to be extremely low‑quality. Because of this, I’ve started to dislike searching for worlds.\n\nI also feel that more and more worlds are using AI‑generated thumbnails or images that have nothing to do with the actual world.\n\nOn top of that, I’m getting tired of seeing many worlds that reuse the same world assets (such as buildings).\n\nSo I would like the system to allow creators to register multiple images taken inside the world, not just a single thumbnail.\n\nI’m sure I’m not the only one who feels this way.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "World Thumbnail Addition Feature",
